From 9d5d4a43b7a9a75a4149a534d99a063b5e3b20ab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 07:41:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] placement forwarder: a rejected hub request is
 terminal, never a clock park

Incident placement:worker-2:b80b2c801dd844db7b56cbf4 (card t_01a1ce825d4f4a54): the MacBook
rejected the forwarded copy with create_overlap 8.5 s after it was sent. The only match it named
was the forwarding card itself, the local placeholder that the target sees through the hub replica.
Forwarder.run/_await only treated `done` as terminal (remote_task_id), so await_task_id returned
None and the card was re-parked on the REQUEUE_SECONDS clock every 10 minutes, forever.

- kanban_placement: FAILED_STATES (rejected/expired/failed, hermes-hub's terminal non-done
  states) and remote_rejection(rid), which parses the target's `kanban create --json` refusal
  out of the stored result (code, matches, total_matches, note). await_task_id stops
  waiting as soon as the request has failed.
- Forwarder._forward: when the client carries options, send distinct_from=[local card id] +
  distinct_reason, so the receiver's overlap guard never self-matches the placeholder. A client
  that rejects the option as create_option_unknown still gets the plain forward. The request id is
  derived from the transport key, so in-flight forwards keep their ids.
- Forwarder._await: a failed request goes to _rejected instead of a clock park (checked before the
  45 s wait and after it). A create_overlap that names only this card is re-forwarded once with
  distinct_from under a new transport key (`...:distinct`, so a new request id) and recorded as
  reforwarded/reforward_of. An overlap with another card, or with hidden matches
  (total_matches > shown), blocks for a decision and ends the deferral. Anything else, including
  a second self-match or an old client that cannot send distinct_from, cancels the deferral
  (placement_deferred_cancelled), so the card runs here.

Proof: new tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_placement_rejected.py (the test_kanban_placement.py facade
is at its 2000-line cap). (a) A rejected sent row never yields a `scheduled` event, either on wake
or during the first wait, for self-overlap, other-overlap and plain rejections.
(b) A self-match overlap re-forwards once with distinct_from under a new request id, and a second
self-match does not forward a third time. 9 hand mutants of the new conditions all killed.
Replay on worker-2's hub replica: of the sent rows (52 done, 2 rejected), exactly one placement
request is non-done, the incident row. Only its handling changes: a re-forward with
distinct_from. The other rejected row is not a placement request.
Placement suites (placement, _cancel, _identity, origin_notify, lockguard, watcher, ...) pass:
377 tests.
